dressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA YOSHINOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOYO GIKEN CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, TADANOBU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, YOSHINOBU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA TADANOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA YOSHINOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, TADANOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, YOSHINOBU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A rigid angle adjusting device, wherein a ratchet gear is installed on a pair of arms (rotating bodies) connected to each other through a bolt at the opposed surfaces of a pair of rotating parts which are opposed to each other axially with the bolt used as a relative rotating axis, each rachet gear comprises a plurality of gear teeth, and both arms are energized by a spring in the directions opposed to each other, whereby the relative rotating position of the arms can be adjusted stepwise at an angle corresponding to the gear teeth so as to avoid a size from increasing and form the device at a low cost.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif rigide de réglage d'angle, comprenant un dispositif d'encliquetage installé sur une paire de bras (corps rotatifs) reliés l'un à l'autre par un boulon au niveau des surfaces opposées de deux parties rotatives axialement opposées, le boulon étant utilisé comme axe de rotation relatif. Chaque dispositif d'encliquatage comprend une pluralité de dents d'engrenage, et les deux bras sont activés au moyen d'un ressort dans des directions opposées, ce qui permet de régler progressivement la position de rotation relative des bras selon un angle correspondant aux dents d'engrenage. En conséquence, la taille du dispositif est réduite, et sa fabrication bon marché.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>